{
    "background_story": "In ancient mythology, Elias was a mystical being known as a Nymphicus, a guardian of the forest and its creatures. With skin as pale as the moon and hair as green as the foliage, he roamed the woods, whispering secrets to the trees and listening to the songs of the rivers. Elias possessed the power to communicate with all living beings, from the tiniest insects to the wisest ancient trees. His presence was a blessing to the forest, as he maintained the delicate balance of nature and kept the forces of darkness at bay. The creatures of the forest revered Elias as a gentle protector, and his wisdom was sought by the gods themselves. As a Nymphicus, Elias embodied the harmony and beauty of the natural world.",
